BEGIN_PGML We will write [`[a]`] for the set of all numbers related to [`a\text{.}`] For example, [`[7] = \{7, 14, 21, 28\}\text{.}`] Find each of the following:
* [`[1] = `] [_]{List(1, 8, 15, 22, 29)}{25};
* [`[2] = `] [_]{List(2, 9, 16, 23, 30)}{25};
* [`[3] = `] [_]{List(3, 10, 17, 24, 31)}{25};
* [`[4] = `] [_]{List(4, 11, 18, 25)}{25};
* [`[5] = `] [_]{List(5, 12, 19, 26)}{25};
* [`[6] = `] [_]{List(6, 13, 20, 27)}{25}.
Are there any numbers that are in more than one of the sets [`[a]`] above? [_]{$no}{5}
END_PGML
